  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 257 AM CDT Fri Jul 10 2026\n\nPrecipitation lingers into Saturday as an upper-level shortwave \nkeeps supporting development. There is currently a Marginal risk \n(level 1/5) from the SPC for severe storms Saturday, though a Slight \nrisk lies against our border to the south. This is a result of the \ngenerally zonal pattern not acting to move the stalled boundary, and \nwe will see what is hopefully a lower-magnitude echo of Friday's \nactivity.\n\nHeading into Sunday, precipitation finally comes to an end by midday \nas building high pressure to the north finally dislodges the \nboundary to the south. Through the rest of the period, \nprecipitation potential comes in the form of isolated afternoon \nsummer thunderstorms with less than 20% chance of occurrence.\n\nBroad upper-level ridging begins to build in early next week, \nallowing for a slow warming trend of a degree or two per day until \nhighs return to around 90 by the end of the week. However, longer \nterm guidance is suggesting the potential for a return to \nuncomfortable heat after the next week.",
